WEBVTT

00:00:11.750 --> 00:00:14.040
"Celebrating 15 years of GINTAMA anime"

00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:17.080
"Presented by GINTAMA
Theatrical Production Committee"

00:00:41.410 --> 00:00:42.790
The land of the samurai.

00:00:43.950 --> 00:00:48.950
There was a time, long ago,
when our country was called by that name.

00:00:59.750 --> 00:01:04.660
Those dream-filled blue skies upon
which the samurai once gazed

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:07.250
are now filled with ships
from strange worlds.

00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:12.950
The streets where the samurai
once proudly walked

00:01:13.290 --> 00:01:15.870
are now filled with swaggering,
arrogant aliens.

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:18.540
Hey, dammit!

00:01:19.910 --> 00:01:22.160
But a select few rose up
to face this crisis,

00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:24.540
one unprecedented in the Edo of old...

00:01:25.540 --> 00:01:27.160
They were the samurai.

00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:28.830
No...

00:01:33.950 --> 00:01:36.250
They were the Z Warriors!

00:01:50.450 --> 00:01:55.040
- Part 1: The Super Long Story!
- "Part 1: The Super Long Story"

00:01:56.080 --> 00:01:58.950
So, planets out there in the universe
have a thing called Altana,

00:01:59.080 --> 00:02:02.040
a sort of energy that's like
that world's life force.

00:02:02.410 --> 00:02:05.040
On Earth, it's also known as ley lines.

00:02:05.370 --> 00:02:10.200
That energy led to the birth
of the immortal fiend known as Utsuro.

00:02:10.910 --> 00:02:15.330
As a result of living life after life,
an existence of never-ending suffering,

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:17.450
Utsuro developed multiple
separate personalities.

00:02:17.950 --> 00:02:20.200
One of these was teacher
of Gintoki and the others

00:02:20.500 --> 00:02:22.160
and founder of the Shoka Sonjuku school,

00:02:22.290 --> 00:02:24.200
Shoyo Yoshida.

00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:27.330
With the goal of destroying
the entire planet, himself included,

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:30.160
Utsuro waged war
against the known universe.

00:02:31.540 --> 00:02:35.120
The people of Edo
resisted with all their might,

00:02:35.950 --> 00:02:37.370
and at the end of a fierce battle,

00:02:37.450 --> 00:02:39.950
the Odd Jobs and their allies
showed real strength

00:02:40.700 --> 00:02:44.620
and forced Utsuro to fall
into the ley lines.

00:02:45.700 --> 00:02:49.120
It was then that, having used up all
his energy to contain the ley lines,

00:02:49.250 --> 00:02:52.950
the dog deity called Sadaharu
entered a long coma.

00:02:54.080 --> 00:02:55.700
Later, the members of the Odd Jobs

00:02:55.870 --> 00:03:00.370
found their respective goals
and set off on their own paths.

00:03:03.330 --> 00:03:06.790
- "Two Years Later"
- And so, two years passed...

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:11.700
I'm gonna do it!

00:03:12.620 --> 00:03:15.580
I will become the Pirate King!

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:17.870
Huh? No, wait.

00:03:17.950 --> 00:03:19.950
Not that "two years later."

00:03:20.290 --> 00:03:23.040
We've done so many
two- and five-year timeskips,

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:25.660
it's hard to keep the story
straight at this point.

00:03:25.910 --> 00:03:27.700
Ah, here! This is it!

00:03:29.580 --> 00:03:30.910
Let's see...

00:03:31.580 --> 00:03:35.250
Kagura looked to find a way
to return Sadaharu to normal,

00:03:35.410 --> 00:03:37.500
while Shinpachi remained in Edo.

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:41.450
Meanwhile, Gintoki,
having foreseen Utsuro's return,

00:03:41.620 --> 00:03:44.700
made the rounds of the gates,
the openings in various, scattered areas

00:03:44.830 --> 00:03:46.750
from which the ley lines' power erupts.

00:03:47.370 --> 00:03:51.410
Utsuro's genes continued to survive
deep underground within the ley lines.

00:03:51.580 --> 00:03:54.120
Over two years,
they rebuilt his physical form,

00:03:54.330 --> 00:03:56.500
and he was reborn at a remote ley line.

00:03:57.330 --> 00:04:01.080
Gintoki wandered the lands with Utsuro,
who grew rapidly, in tow.

00:04:01.870 --> 00:04:04.160
One day, it became clear that the body

00:04:04.250 --> 00:04:06.540
housed a personality
that could be Shoyo.

00:04:08.620 --> 00:04:12.580
However, Utsuro was captured
by the Death Star Sect,

00:04:12.790 --> 00:04:14.790
led by the remnants of the Tendoshuu.

00:04:15.580 --> 00:04:18.250
To prevent them from gaining
a perfect immortal,

00:04:18.450 --> 00:04:22.450
he left his heart alone with Gintoki.

00:04:23.160 --> 00:04:26.370
In order to complete Utsuro's recovery,

00:04:26.830 --> 00:04:30.660
and by extension their own immortality,

00:04:30.950 --> 00:04:33.540
the Sect sets its sights on Earth's Altana.

00:04:34.410 --> 00:04:38.330
At the ruins of the Shoka Sonjuku,
Gintoki is reunited with Takasugi,

00:04:38.540 --> 00:04:40.830
who has used the bones
of senior student Oboro

00:04:40.910 --> 00:04:42.750
to become partially immortal.

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:45.290
In order to thwart the Sect's plans,

00:04:45.450 --> 00:04:47.790
Gintoki and Takasugi head for Edo.

00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:50.950
Upon returning to Edo,

00:04:51.250 --> 00:04:53.540
Gintoki spots the older
Shinpachi and Kagura

00:04:53.830 --> 00:04:55.330
but doesn't make contact.

00:04:56.620 --> 00:04:59.290
Meanwhile, Katsura, the first Prime Minister,

00:04:59.500 --> 00:05:03.120
uses his office to investigate
the Sect's actions.

00:05:04.250 --> 00:05:06.160
In order to draw out the Sect,

00:05:06.330 --> 00:05:09.620
Takasugi blows up the Terminal
and attempts to assassinate Katsura.

00:05:10.580 --> 00:05:11.950
Katsura uses the assassination as cover

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:14.500
to relinquish his
position as Prime Minister.

00:05:15.160 --> 00:05:18.870
The pupils of the Shoka Sonjuku school
once again come together.

00:05:19.700 --> 00:05:20.750
Even the Shinsengumi,

00:05:20.830 --> 00:05:23.910
who were pretending to
have disbanded, regroup.

00:05:24.910 --> 00:05:28.040
Meanwhile, the gorilla was holding
a wedding ceremony.

00:05:29.700 --> 00:05:32.450
After much ado, the ship carrying Kondo

00:05:32.620 --> 00:05:36.200
attacks the Sect's Mobile Cathedral Kuyo,

00:05:36.540 --> 00:05:39.040
causing the wreckage
to fall atop the Terminal.

00:05:39.450 --> 00:05:41.500
Kondo reunites with the Shinsengumi.

00:05:42.910 --> 00:05:45.830
However, the Sect occupies the Terminal,

00:05:45.950 --> 00:05:48.540
and the city is plunged into danger.

00:05:49.330 --> 00:05:51.330
Edo is once again faced with harm.

00:05:52.040 --> 00:05:54.200
This is when Shinpachi, Kagura,

00:05:54.540 --> 00:05:58.330
and the residents of Kabuki District
gather in front of Odd Jobs

00:05:58.950 --> 00:06:00.950
and set off to battle.

00:06:02.500 --> 00:06:08.790
To fulfill the wishes of,
and save, their teacher,

00:06:09.200 --> 00:06:11.370
Gintoki, Takasugi, and Katsura
decide to rescue Utsuro.

00:06:11.620 --> 00:06:13.790
The Terminal would be the battlefield.

00:06:14.660 --> 00:06:20.040
Will the Z Warriors be able
to reclaim the future?

00:06:20.200 --> 00:06:23.500
Nobody could pay attention
to the recap with those visuals!

00:06:26.410 --> 00:06:28.700
- Wolf Fang Fist!
- "Wolf Fang Fist"

00:06:30.950 --> 00:06:33.250
Not only was it way too long,

00:06:33.370 --> 00:06:36.370
the art style made it look like
it was for a completely different show!

00:06:36.580 --> 00:06:38.950
It looked like some
fan-made Dragon Ball anime!

00:06:39.160 --> 00:06:42.330
Dragen Bell?
What are you talking about, Katsurass?

00:06:42.450 --> 00:06:44.830
I'm not Katsurass! I'm Katsura!

00:06:45.500 --> 00:06:49.410
So the anime staff have finally
gotten serious, huh?

00:06:49.950 --> 00:06:52.290
Free from the shackles of TV production,

00:06:52.410 --> 00:06:55.500
they've finally started putting
some effort into the animation.

00:06:56.160 --> 00:06:58.750
This is what the animation staff
are truly capable of.

00:06:58.870 --> 00:07:02.040
They're just drawing while holding
Dragon Balls in their left hands!

00:07:02.410 --> 00:07:05.410
And why do I have to be Yamcha
while this fool is Vegeta?!

00:07:05.620 --> 00:07:08.080
That makes me look like a total loser!

00:07:08.700 --> 00:07:10.830
So stupid! I'm not playing
along with your nonsense.

00:07:10.950 --> 00:07:13.250
It pains me to say it,
but you're virtually identical.

00:07:13.370 --> 00:07:15.950
And when did you become a master
at growing a widow's peak?

00:07:16.040 --> 00:07:18.290
You guys just don't get it, do you?

00:07:18.750 --> 00:07:20.950
We've gone beyond
the final TV episode,

00:07:21.200 --> 00:07:23.370
beyond the manga's ending scams,

00:07:23.500 --> 00:07:25.660
and finally reached this point...

00:07:26.200 --> 00:07:28.870
this new world: the movie theater!

00:07:31.370 --> 00:07:34.450
And it's up to us to show
those in attendance here today...

00:07:35.750 --> 00:07:39.250
our power, and the power
of Akira Toriyama!

00:07:39.540 --> 00:07:42.450
Shoyo, looks like things
worked out somehow, huh?

00:07:42.750 --> 00:07:45.080
Yes! No matter what anyone says,

00:07:45.290 --> 00:07:47.620
things did work out somehow!

00:07:48.160 --> 00:07:50.620
Got that right!

00:07:53.620 --> 00:07:56.410
And this marks the end
of the cinematic exploits

00:07:56.700 --> 00:07:58.830
of Gintoki and his companions.

00:07:59.250 --> 00:08:02.790
Their path ahead is sure to be
rife with trials and tribulations,

00:08:03.080 --> 00:08:05.540
but they will no doubt
be able to overcome them.

00:08:05.870 --> 00:08:10.620
They will be fine,
for they have the Silver Balls.

00:08:11.950 --> 00:08:13.950
What the hell are Silver Balls?

00:08:15.660 --> 00:08:17.250
Galick Gun!

00:08:17.870 --> 00:08:19.620
Kakarot!

00:08:19.950 --> 00:08:22.200
Are they balls that can grant wishes?

00:08:22.410 --> 00:08:26.120
Or are they the same as
the pea you call a brain?

00:08:26.580 --> 00:08:28.830
If balls that convenient really existed,

00:08:29.290 --> 00:08:33.830
none of us would be here
in this position right now.

00:08:47.160 --> 00:08:49.950
And yet, I'd like to be grateful.

00:08:50.910 --> 00:08:55.500
We managed to get this far
on our own two feet.

00:09:02.660 --> 00:09:04.660
With our own power,

00:09:07.410 --> 00:09:08.830
with these very hands of ours...

00:09:09.040 --> 00:09:11.040
we will take back everything...

00:09:12.290 --> 00:09:14.040
we lost.

00:09:14.620 --> 00:09:19.250
That's how we, the students of Shoyo,
do things, right?

00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:26.290
"GINTAMA"

00:09:26.410 --> 00:09:32.080
"Part 2: Fate"

00:11:14.080 --> 00:11:15.620
Fire!

00:11:31.950 --> 00:11:33.120
Eliminate them!

00:11:33.250 --> 00:11:35.330
Bring the hammer down upon those heretics

00:11:35.450 --> 00:11:37.660
who would interfere
with our divine summon...

00:11:38.580 --> 00:11:40.080
Divine summoning?

00:11:40.250 --> 00:11:45.160
That's rich, coming from a bunch of fools
looking for immortality on the cheap!

00:11:50.830 --> 00:11:53.580
Look.
Their ship is down,

00:11:53.700 --> 00:11:55.700
but it's still drawing
Altana from the Earth

00:11:55.870 --> 00:11:58.450
through the Terminal's core.

00:12:00.250 --> 00:12:03.580
The Seireimon Gate is still operating?

00:12:04.250 --> 00:12:05.870
And with that Altana,

00:12:06.200 --> 00:12:08.580
even an incomplete god without a heart

00:12:08.750 --> 00:12:11.120
can be brought back to life?

00:12:15.870 --> 00:12:18.450
I'm more surprised
that so many people

00:12:18.540 --> 00:12:20.950
want to live forever
in this awful world.

00:12:21.540 --> 00:12:24.620
My life has put me through
more than enough joys and sorrows.

00:12:24.950 --> 00:12:28.450
If I can overcome that last,
final trial with you all...

00:12:33.040 --> 00:12:36.830
I won't mind if my life
is to end right here!

00:12:41.830 --> 00:12:45.080
Would our meeting be one of the joys?

00:12:46.620 --> 00:12:48.410
Or is it one of the sorrows?

00:12:49.910 --> 00:12:51.910
There's no telling at this point,

00:12:53.290 --> 00:12:56.580
but there is one thing that's for sure...

00:13:09.700 --> 00:13:11.910
We hated and tried to kill each other,

00:13:12.870 --> 00:13:14.870
but still our ties couldn't be broken.

00:13:16.750 --> 00:13:18.950
I'm sick of you idiots,

00:13:19.750 --> 00:13:22.700
and I'm sick of being
given the runaround by you fools.

00:13:23.080 --> 00:13:26.370
I sure hope this life is
the last one you ruin for me!

00:13:32.750 --> 00:13:33.950
That so?

00:13:34.290 --> 00:13:35.950
Too bad for you, though.

00:13:36.370 --> 00:13:38.450
You guys can't die just yet.

00:13:40.450 --> 00:13:42.200
I won't let you.

00:13:44.750 --> 00:13:46.950
I get how they feel.

00:13:47.870 --> 00:13:51.120
I don't want to die.
I want to keep on living.

00:13:57.370 --> 00:14:00.830
Because there's this fool of a teacher
who's put me through so much,

00:14:01.200 --> 00:14:03.790
and this other idiot who just threw me
like a sack of potatoes,

00:14:04.330 --> 00:14:06.910
and I'm not done beating them up.

00:14:07.080 --> 00:14:10.700
I have some things
I'd like to say to Sensei as well.

00:14:11.080 --> 00:14:12.790
Same here. A great many things.

00:14:12.910 --> 00:14:15.450
How long will you have to
beat him up to feel better?

00:14:26.910 --> 00:14:30.330
An eternity wouldn't be long enough!

00:14:49.120 --> 00:14:50.330
Zura!

00:15:06.160 --> 00:15:09.580
To the people occupying the Terminal

00:15:09.950 --> 00:15:13.160
you are completely surrounded.

00:15:13.580 --> 00:15:15.620
Resistance is futile.

00:15:16.160 --> 00:15:17.790
Give yourselves up now!

00:15:18.080 --> 00:15:20.040
If you don't...

00:15:21.750 --> 00:15:22.950
Shoot them down!

00:15:27.290 --> 00:15:29.620
If you don't,

00:15:30.370 --> 00:15:32.410
let me express my gratitude.

00:15:33.120 --> 00:15:34.870
Thanks to you all,

00:15:35.200 --> 00:15:39.250
our country has become this strong!

00:15:47.830 --> 00:15:49.830
Go!

00:15:58.500 --> 00:15:59.620
Those guys...

00:16:00.080 --> 00:16:01.290
Let's go!

00:16:02.950 --> 00:16:07.410
Decades have passed
since you Amanto came to Earth.

00:16:07.790 --> 00:16:09.200
We have lived

00:16:09.500 --> 00:16:12.040
lives full of doubt and agony!

00:16:13.040 --> 00:16:14.870
But now we can say this...

00:16:15.750 --> 00:16:18.870
those days have not been in vain!

00:16:21.830 --> 00:16:23.870
Amidst all that we've lost,

00:16:24.120 --> 00:16:26.120
we have found that which is important

00:16:26.330 --> 00:16:28.120
that which we must protect!

00:16:29.660 --> 00:16:31.250
Our shadows on the ground

00:16:31.910 --> 00:16:34.290
have showed us the way to the light!

00:16:38.120 --> 00:16:40.790
So we won't fear you anymore.

00:16:41.580 --> 00:16:44.580
We'll meet you head on,
fair and square!

00:16:55.330 --> 00:16:57.830
- Welcome to the land of the samurai.
- Welcome to the land of the samurai.

00:17:02.540 --> 00:17:04.910
A land whose people possess
minds of steel...

00:17:05.620 --> 00:17:08.700
A land whose people
possess souls of silver.

00:17:10.370 --> 00:17:12.040
- We're glad to have you!
- We're glad to have you!

00:17:36.370 --> 00:17:37.700
Gintoki!

00:17:42.120 --> 00:17:43.410
Gintoki!

00:17:52.080 --> 00:17:54.410
Pops! We could use some help!

00:17:54.580 --> 00:17:58.500
Split up the enemy's defenses
around the Terminal!

00:17:58.830 --> 00:18:01.040
Screw that tedious crap.

00:18:01.410 --> 00:18:04.330
We'll just attack the mothership on top!

00:18:04.580 --> 00:18:05.830
Right now, that ship

00:18:05.950 --> 00:18:08.950
contains all the Altana
it's taken in from the Terminal!

00:18:09.290 --> 00:18:12.700
If you attack it now,
there's no telling what will happen.

00:18:12.870 --> 00:18:14.790
Just leave it to us!

00:18:21.790 --> 00:18:23.700
Yo. You took your time.

00:18:23.790 --> 00:18:25.120
You took so long,

00:18:25.250 --> 00:18:28.080
I thought you guys had
turned tail and run for it.

00:18:28.410 --> 00:18:31.830
Can't have a party without
the guests of honor,

00:18:32.330 --> 00:18:34.330
- know what I'm saying?
- Well, well...

00:18:34.750 --> 00:18:38.870
So you finally admit that
the Odd Jobs are better than you, huh?

00:18:39.540 --> 00:18:41.250
The hell are you talking about?

00:18:41.540 --> 00:18:43.540
I'm just saying,
if we're gonna raise hell,

00:18:44.370 --> 00:18:47.040
it'd be more fun to do it

00:18:47.910 --> 00:18:49.700
with the most nasty devils around.

00:18:49.830 --> 00:18:52.620
I guess that means we're out, then.

00:18:56.080 --> 00:18:57.370
Let's go...

00:18:57.950 --> 00:18:59.790
To see our guests of honor,

00:19:01.620 --> 00:19:03.620
and raise hell one last time!

00:19:06.870 --> 00:19:10.250
This is shaping up to be
a long, dragged-out battle.

00:19:10.660 --> 00:19:12.330
We should fall back and regroup.

00:19:12.540 --> 00:19:14.580
Even if we do succeed in reviving Utsuro,

00:19:14.700 --> 00:19:17.620
it would be for naught
if we lost the Sect in the process.

00:19:17.910 --> 00:19:22.540
We'd lose the ability to produce the elixir
and our chance to return to power.

00:19:23.080 --> 00:19:25.080
No need to worry.

00:19:25.200 --> 00:19:27.160
Everything is going as planned.

00:19:27.620 --> 00:19:29.120
It really does seem as though Utsuro

00:19:29.250 --> 00:19:32.160
can only be fueled
by the Altana on Earth.

00:19:32.790 --> 00:19:37.120
Look! Our god is truly pleased!

00:19:39.250 --> 00:19:41.160
Is the Altana he's absorbing...

00:19:41.370 --> 00:19:44.580
...reconstructing his heart?

00:19:45.790 --> 00:19:48.830
The time is nigh.
Very soon,

00:19:50.620 --> 00:19:52.200
our god will awaken.

00:19:52.410 --> 00:19:54.160
Isn't that enough?

00:19:54.290 --> 00:19:57.500
Prolonging this any further
will make it harder for us to leave.

00:19:57.950 --> 00:19:59.950
Prepare to withdraw!

00:20:05.950 --> 00:20:08.700
You cannot control
your bodies, is it?

00:20:09.580 --> 00:20:11.410
It happened to me too.

00:20:12.410 --> 00:20:16.540
We Tendoshu self-destructed
by stealing Utsuro's blood,

00:20:17.120 --> 00:20:20.160
but that very same blood
brought us back.

00:20:21.620 --> 00:20:25.080
We were being kept alive,
being used,

00:20:27.160 --> 00:20:28.870
and being controlled

00:20:29.040 --> 00:20:31.950
by Utsuro's genes
from the moment we took them in.

00:20:40.040 --> 00:20:42.950
We have always been a
part of Utsuro.

00:20:44.580 --> 00:20:47.580
And now it falls upon us
to execute his will.

00:21:31.870 --> 00:21:33.790
Hand over the heart.

00:21:34.040 --> 00:21:36.450
It doesn't belong in your hands.

00:21:37.080 --> 00:21:39.500
They are meant to hold better things.

00:21:42.830 --> 00:21:44.830
Since we had the same teacher,

00:21:45.700 --> 00:21:48.410
you and I were fated to cross swords.

00:21:51.750 --> 00:21:53.830
If I could do it all over again...

00:21:54.250 --> 00:21:55.370
I...

00:21:56.870 --> 00:21:58.870
I would've loved to be
one of you guys...

00:22:02.160 --> 00:22:03.660
I have my own,

00:22:04.200 --> 00:22:05.950
and you have your own

00:22:06.410 --> 00:22:07.830
things to take back, right?

00:22:12.450 --> 00:22:13.540
Takasugi,

00:22:14.200 --> 00:22:15.330
I...

00:22:44.700 --> 00:22:46.080
Let's get a move on.

00:22:50.040 --> 00:22:52.290
- Takasugi.
- What?

00:22:52.410 --> 00:22:56.500
There's nothing left for me
to take back.

00:22:58.500 --> 00:23:01.620
Whatever I lost
has come back to me.

00:23:02.410 --> 00:23:04.410
It's all right here.

00:23:05.330 --> 00:23:09.330
And I'm here to make sure
I don't lose any of it ever again.

00:23:17.830 --> 00:23:19.830
Gintoki! Takasugi!

00:23:23.250 --> 00:23:24.870
Zura!

00:23:27.080 --> 00:23:28.790
Jump!

00:23:38.250 --> 00:23:39.580
You're stepping on me.

00:23:41.250 --> 00:23:43.120
Now we're even.

00:23:43.620 --> 00:23:46.500
You're the last person
I wanna owe anything.

00:23:46.870 --> 00:23:49.410
What a coincidence.
I could say the same...

00:23:55.750 --> 00:23:57.620
Takasugi?

00:24:03.160 --> 00:24:06.910
It's over.
You people cannot beat me.

00:24:11.620 --> 00:24:15.040
Did you catch a glimpse of
the Utsuro within me?

00:24:19.080 --> 00:24:21.580
Utsuro rules over and decides all.

00:24:21.790 --> 00:24:23.700
His designs are inescapable...

00:24:24.040 --> 00:24:25.750
Just like fate.

00:24:32.950 --> 00:24:34.290
That so?

00:24:34.450 --> 00:24:36.080
Is this what you're telling me, then?

00:24:36.450 --> 00:24:40.370
That I'm only standing here, undying,

00:24:40.750 --> 00:24:42.750
because Utsuro led me here?

00:24:43.750 --> 00:24:45.120
Wrong.

00:24:45.410 --> 00:24:46.500
I...

00:24:46.700 --> 00:24:48.370
We weren't led here by anyone.

00:24:48.620 --> 00:24:50.910
We stand before you
of our own free will.

00:25:17.790 --> 00:25:19.080
Go!

00:25:27.950 --> 00:25:29.950
I'm taking this back.

00:25:46.370 --> 00:25:48.870
You are... Hitsugi, was it?

00:25:49.620 --> 00:25:52.620
One of the Three Crows
in Tenshoin Naraku.

00:25:53.250 --> 00:25:54.750
Why would you go so far?

00:25:54.950 --> 00:25:57.830
Why do you want the heart of
your former chief, Utsuro, so badly?

00:26:41.620 --> 00:26:44.200
Hand over the heart.

00:27:31.080 --> 00:27:32.370
Kagura!

00:27:39.750 --> 00:27:40.910
Kagura!

00:27:41.450 --> 00:27:44.450
I'm fine! Go on ahead!

00:28:11.660 --> 00:28:15.410
Hand over... the heart!

00:28:16.160 --> 00:28:17.370
Why?

00:28:17.500 --> 00:28:20.540
Naraku has already fallen apart
as an organization!

00:28:22.790 --> 00:28:24.750
And yet you still want
to bring Utsuro back,

00:28:24.870 --> 00:28:28.410
even if you have to reduce
Edo to rabble?

00:28:44.410 --> 00:28:46.040
The only one...

00:28:46.500 --> 00:28:48.580
The only one who can save him...

00:28:48.950 --> 00:28:51.080
is me!

00:29:09.330 --> 00:29:10.580
You...

00:29:11.120 --> 00:29:12.620
Don't tell me...

00:29:45.040 --> 00:29:47.160
Make use of me.

00:29:47.540 --> 00:29:49.040
You...

00:30:18.620 --> 00:30:19.750
It's futile.

00:30:20.120 --> 00:30:22.500
You can't take us down
with your inferior blood.

00:30:22.830 --> 00:30:24.750
Die.

00:30:32.500 --> 00:30:36.580
Then let's go ahead and see
whose blood, mine or yours,

00:30:36.950 --> 00:30:39.040
will dry up first.

00:30:39.160 --> 00:30:41.160
This will go right down to the wire.

00:30:45.330 --> 00:30:46.540
Do it.

00:30:53.750 --> 00:30:55.120
What's going on?

00:31:18.290 --> 00:31:20.290
Gintoki...

00:31:28.250 --> 00:31:29.580
How foolish!

00:31:29.700 --> 00:31:31.620
Unable to watch
your friend sacrifice himself,

00:31:31.830 --> 00:31:34.580
you lost a golden opportunity
to take me down.

00:31:35.910 --> 00:31:38.910
That sort of miracle won't
ever happen for you again!

00:31:39.250 --> 00:31:41.410
Gin!

00:31:44.290 --> 00:31:45.540
Hey.

00:31:45.660 --> 00:31:48.410
No need to scream.
I can hear you just fine.

00:31:52.620 --> 00:31:55.620
Curse you!

00:32:04.330 --> 00:32:05.580
Sadaharu?

00:32:05.950 --> 00:32:07.450
Sadaharu!

00:32:10.120 --> 00:32:12.330
Sadaharu!

00:32:27.080 --> 00:32:28.700
Sadaharu...

00:32:29.540 --> 00:32:33.540
You've been waiting to meet Gin
just like us, haven't you?

00:32:34.620 --> 00:32:36.160
Sadaharu...

00:32:42.080 --> 00:32:44.040
Sadaharu!

00:32:50.040 --> 00:32:52.580
S... Sadaharu.

00:32:52.950 --> 00:32:55.950
You've finally come back to us.

00:32:56.410 --> 00:32:57.910
To help us...

00:32:58.250 --> 00:33:00.500
To help Gin.

00:33:03.290 --> 00:33:06.040
- Sadaharu!
- Something came out!

00:33:06.200 --> 00:33:08.370
Hold it! Sadaharu's back,

00:33:08.540 --> 00:33:11.330
but did he just... eat Gin?

00:33:11.540 --> 00:33:13.040
Did he swallow him whole?

00:33:13.200 --> 00:33:14.370
It's understandable.

00:33:14.580 --> 00:33:17.500
Sadaharu just recovered.
He needs nutrition.

00:33:17.620 --> 00:33:20.540
He didn't come to help, then.
He just showed up 'cause he was hungry!

00:33:20.620 --> 00:33:22.950
Don't worry. Gin's a piece of trash.

00:33:23.080 --> 00:33:25.660
Can't be digested.
He'll show up soon enough.

00:33:25.790 --> 00:33:27.080
Gin!

00:33:27.160 --> 00:33:29.370
What kind of hell reunion is this?

00:33:29.450 --> 00:33:31.700
Gin... Gin!

00:33:35.910 --> 00:33:37.330
What do you want?

00:33:37.790 --> 00:33:41.080
Sorry. Got the wrong guy.

00:33:44.910 --> 00:33:47.580
Some complete random
just came out of there!

00:33:47.750 --> 00:33:49.250
And went right back!

00:33:49.330 --> 00:33:52.750
A parasite, maybe.
He's always eaten stuff off the ground.

00:33:52.870 --> 00:33:56.620
What kind of parasite
looks like it needs to pay rent?

00:33:58.540 --> 00:34:00.870
That was a great bath.

00:34:01.040 --> 00:34:02.950
They're coming out one after another!

00:34:03.040 --> 00:34:06.580
What's this, a bathhouse?
Is there an entire world in there?

00:34:07.330 --> 00:34:10.910
Excuse me! Did you happen to see
a silver-haired man inside?

00:34:11.160 --> 00:34:12.790
Silver-haired?

00:34:13.040 --> 00:34:15.790
Oh, you mean the newbie?

00:34:16.790 --> 00:34:21.580
That kid took a different exit,
saying he didn't wanna be covered in filth.

00:34:22.330 --> 00:34:24.330
He was covered in filth anyway!

00:34:28.620 --> 00:34:29.830
Gin...

00:34:29.910 --> 00:34:31.870
Remember what I said?

00:34:32.500 --> 00:34:36.950
If you ever found something you really
needed to do, I'd close up shop?

00:34:38.620 --> 00:34:40.450
Does the fact that you're here...

00:34:40.750 --> 00:34:43.660
mean that you've gone back
to having nothing?

00:34:44.500 --> 00:34:45.620
No.

00:34:46.160 --> 00:34:49.620
We're here for something
we need to do.

00:34:50.410 --> 00:34:55.950
Gin, we weren't Odd Jobs
because we had nothing to do.

00:34:57.750 --> 00:34:59.750
We were just fine with anything.

00:35:00.290 --> 00:35:01.950
We were fine with anything...

00:35:03.410 --> 00:35:05.330
As long as we could be here

00:35:05.830 --> 00:35:07.830
with you and everyone else.

00:35:08.910 --> 00:35:10.450
That's why we will...

00:35:10.790 --> 00:35:12.750
always be Odd Jobs!

00:35:14.250 --> 00:35:15.580
Sheesh.

00:35:15.750 --> 00:35:20.830
You've gone and grown so much
in the time I was gone.

00:35:23.540 --> 00:35:24.870
My back hurts.

00:35:25.370 --> 00:35:27.290
Mind giving me a hand?

00:35:28.410 --> 00:35:30.620
Come on, you sound pathetic.

00:35:31.120 --> 00:35:32.830
And you call yourself Odd Jobs?

00:35:32.950 --> 00:35:35.250
Surely your list of services
includes compassion?

00:35:35.500 --> 00:35:37.370
Give me an employee's discount.

00:35:37.700 --> 00:35:40.200
Apparently, it's not that we've grown.

00:35:40.410 --> 00:35:42.200
Gin's just regressed.

00:35:42.410 --> 00:35:43.620
Completely

00:35:49.950 --> 00:35:51.950
No, did you shrink for real?

00:35:52.160 --> 00:35:54.250
Hey, you better knock it off.

00:35:54.410 --> 00:35:57.080
Or my long, Shun Oguri legs
will kick your ass.

00:35:57.160 --> 00:35:58.950
More like Short Oguri!

00:35:59.160 --> 00:36:01.790
What's going on? What happened to you?

00:36:01.910 --> 00:36:05.200
Huh? Did I get a little
digested in Sadaharu?

00:36:05.290 --> 00:36:06.450
Digested?

00:36:06.540 --> 00:36:09.120
Did you see anything else come out before me?

00:36:09.950 --> 00:36:11.950
A couple of geezers out of the bath!

00:36:13.040 --> 00:36:15.500
Hey, what do you think you're doing?

00:36:15.620 --> 00:36:17.750
Gintoki Sepia! Gintoki Shepia!

00:36:17.910 --> 00:36:19.200
Sepia? Shepia?

00:36:19.290 --> 00:36:21.620
You can't just split off from me.

00:36:22.080 --> 00:36:24.080
Only when together are we...

00:36:24.950 --> 00:36:27.450
- Ginto3.
- Wait, your name's Ginto3?

00:36:27.500 --> 00:36:30.080
Get back in here!
Gimme back my long legs!

00:36:30.160 --> 00:36:32.660
No way! I'm never going back
to being that awful leg!

00:36:32.790 --> 00:36:35.870
I've always wanted to complain about
you sticking your bare feet in boots!

00:36:35.910 --> 00:36:37.330
What's wrong with him?

00:36:37.450 --> 00:36:40.290
Why's he adding to his character
profile in the final movie?

00:36:42.500 --> 00:36:43.580
That's bad!

00:36:44.450 --> 00:36:46.450
Hurry up, Gin!

00:36:47.080 --> 00:36:49.290
We're right back to square one!

00:36:49.410 --> 00:36:51.370
Pachi-boy, we have no choice.

00:36:51.540 --> 00:36:55.120
We need to get Gintoki Sakata
reconstructed inside of Sadaharu!

00:36:55.290 --> 00:36:56.790
What the heck?

00:36:57.250 --> 00:36:58.290
Oh, jeez!

00:36:58.540 --> 00:37:00.750
Whatever happens, happens!

00:37:03.250 --> 00:37:05.040
- Come back to us,
- Come back to us,

00:37:05.290 --> 00:37:07.620
- Gintoki Sakata!
- Gintoki Sakata!

00:37:15.410 --> 00:37:16.910
That man...

00:37:17.450 --> 00:37:20.290
had eyes too fierce to be a samurai,

00:37:22.580 --> 00:37:26.870
but too focused to be a thug.

00:37:27.950 --> 00:37:29.870
Just like always.

00:38:52.200 --> 00:38:53.450
Are you...

00:38:58.250 --> 00:39:00.250
"Lake Toya"

00:39:06.290 --> 00:39:07.290
Dammit!

00:39:07.370 --> 00:39:09.330
I got all the way up there,

00:39:09.450 --> 00:39:11.450
and I have to do it all over again?

00:39:21.120 --> 00:39:22.620
You seem to be in a hurry.

00:39:23.160 --> 00:39:26.200
I can give you a ride
to the final boss for cheap.

00:39:27.410 --> 00:39:29.370
H-Hero MADAO?

00:39:30.620 --> 00:39:33.790
I quit being the hero.
I'm starting over from scratch again.

00:39:34.620 --> 00:39:37.620
H-Hurry up and get in,
you stupid Earthlings!

00:39:39.160 --> 00:39:41.160
Hey! Let me in!

00:39:46.750 --> 00:39:48.160
-Hey!
-Stay away!

00:39:48.250 --> 00:39:50.250
Let me in if you're in there!

00:40:09.910 --> 00:40:13.910
You people couldn't have done it.

00:40:15.250 --> 00:40:17.620
You finally met your teacher again...

00:40:21.750 --> 00:40:24.700
How could you have put
an end to him?

00:40:25.120 --> 00:40:29.080
You were trying to prevent
Utsuro's return?

00:40:31.950 --> 00:40:33.410
Finally...

00:40:35.200 --> 00:40:37.330
At long last, he can rest.

00:40:40.540 --> 00:40:44.450
Now that I have this body,
which refuses to die even when rotten,

00:40:45.540 --> 00:40:47.700
I finally understood the pain...

00:40:49.200 --> 00:40:51.580
of being eternal...

00:40:55.290 --> 00:40:58.330
I caught just a glimpse
of his deep solitude.

00:41:04.500 --> 00:41:06.870
I pray that at least in the end,

00:41:08.410 --> 00:41:10.540
he can go out humanely.

00:41:53.750 --> 00:41:54.950
Ow...

00:41:55.580 --> 00:41:56.950
Go, quickly!

00:42:37.500 --> 00:42:38.660
Gin!

00:43:07.500 --> 00:43:09.450
Who brought me back?

00:43:09.750 --> 00:43:10.870
Was it you?

00:43:11.830 --> 00:43:13.120
Utsuro...

00:43:13.290 --> 00:43:15.790
I have inherited your blood.

00:43:16.080 --> 00:43:18.410
Wh-What is your desire?

00:43:18.660 --> 00:43:22.370
Revenge on mankind?
The destruction of the universe?

00:43:22.620 --> 00:43:26.620
Whatever it is,
I shall follow you and...

00:43:27.200 --> 00:43:29.620
There is only one thing I desire.

00:43:43.200 --> 00:43:47.620
But it seems I have a job to do first.

00:43:49.540 --> 00:43:50.750
Sensei?

00:44:01.120 --> 00:44:04.450
You're Sensei... right?

00:44:05.620 --> 00:44:08.790
Please don't look so sad.

00:44:09.950 --> 00:44:11.290
I...

00:44:11.620 --> 00:44:15.160
We will protect you
from anything and anyone.

00:44:16.290 --> 00:44:17.410
So please...

00:44:23.290 --> 00:44:25.290
Come back...

00:44:27.040 --> 00:44:31.830
with us... to the Shoka Sonjuku School.

00:44:33.120 --> 00:44:35.200
I have so much...

00:44:36.120 --> 00:44:38.080
so much to tell you.

00:44:38.950 --> 00:44:43.870
And it's my job... to attend to you...

00:44:44.500 --> 00:44:46.540
Sen... sei...

00:44:48.450 --> 00:44:49.450
I...

00:44:50.830 --> 00:44:54.950
I'm not the kind of person
you should call Sensei anymore.

00:44:55.910 --> 00:44:58.950
I can no longer go back
to being Shoyo Yoshida.

00:45:00.700 --> 00:45:01.950
Forgive me.

00:45:03.950 --> 00:45:08.580
You were the ones
I truly wished to protect,

00:45:09.620 --> 00:45:13.870
but I couldn't help a single one of you.

00:45:16.910 --> 00:45:18.040
Forgive me.

00:45:31.700 --> 00:45:34.120
There's no need to apologize.

00:45:35.080 --> 00:45:36.540
Shoyo...

00:45:36.790 --> 00:45:41.910
I knew all along that
you couldn't protect a thing.

00:45:43.450 --> 00:45:46.370
How I waited for this moment.

00:45:46.790 --> 00:45:49.370
Just like you waited
for that one back then,

00:45:50.120 --> 00:45:51.790
I waited for the moment

00:45:51.950 --> 00:45:54.540
you would let your guard down,

00:45:54.830 --> 00:45:56.950
hiding inside...

00:45:57.830 --> 00:45:59.830
this dear pupil of yours.

00:46:23.700 --> 00:46:25.700
Shinpachi! Kagura!

00:46:28.790 --> 00:46:29.790
Damn it all!

00:47:17.410 --> 00:47:18.580
Two years ago,

00:47:18.750 --> 00:47:22.910
as you rejected me and the end,
I believe I gave you some advice.

00:47:23.250 --> 00:47:26.620
So long as you live,
the tragedies will continue to occur.

00:47:27.580 --> 00:47:31.580
I can hear his voice extremely clearly.

00:47:32.870 --> 00:47:35.250
It says he wants to put an end...

00:47:38.200 --> 00:47:40.370
to anything and everything.

00:47:41.410 --> 00:47:44.410
Yeah, I couldn't agree more.

00:47:45.370 --> 00:47:47.250
Let's end this...

00:47:50.250 --> 00:47:51.540
using our swords.

00:47:51.870 --> 00:47:53.870
You still draw that twig?

00:48:25.950 --> 00:48:27.330
Utsuro.

00:48:27.910 --> 00:48:31.910
We may have to put a bunch
of these twigs together to do it,

00:48:32.370 --> 00:48:34.830
but we'll take back
what we lost that day.

00:48:35.790 --> 00:48:37.410
That's a promise.

00:48:37.790 --> 00:48:39.080
It will happen.

00:48:51.040 --> 00:48:54.790
Your little promise
has long been broken.

00:48:55.580 --> 00:48:59.250
By the very man you call your friend.

00:49:04.700 --> 00:49:05.700
Utsuro,

00:49:06.500 --> 00:49:10.120
no matter what tragedies
may befall that guy,

00:49:10.750 --> 00:49:14.290
he's not the type to say
he wants to end things.

00:49:15.790 --> 00:49:19.580
You know what he's more likely
to say at times like these?

00:49:19.910 --> 00:49:23.410
I'll simply destroy...

00:49:23.910 --> 00:49:29.750
this rotten world you
still walk freely upon.

00:50:06.450 --> 00:50:07.620
Utsuro...

00:50:08.160 --> 00:50:11.700
You're not the only one in here.

00:50:24.950 --> 00:50:26.540
Where is Shoyo?

00:50:27.160 --> 00:50:30.160
Where is his corpse?

00:50:32.620 --> 00:50:33.870
A corpse?

00:50:34.620 --> 00:50:36.750
There was never one
here to begin with.

00:50:43.700 --> 00:50:45.700
The one lying flat on the ground

00:50:46.540 --> 00:50:48.540
was you, Utsuro.

00:51:03.870 --> 00:51:05.330
Sensei...

00:51:05.910 --> 00:51:08.290
Problem student that I was,

00:51:08.500 --> 00:51:10.700
it seems I had some homework
left to do.

00:51:12.370 --> 00:51:13.370
Go.

00:51:14.540 --> 00:51:16.290
Don't worry.

00:51:17.040 --> 00:51:19.450
You have many more students

00:51:20.700 --> 00:51:22.500
than just us.

00:51:34.620 --> 00:51:38.620
I'll leave you to them.

00:51:45.540 --> 00:51:48.200
You aren't some immortal
monster anymore.

00:51:49.290 --> 00:51:52.160
The moment you entered his body,
you were done for.

00:51:54.790 --> 00:51:57.700
I'll put an end to you
just like you wish, Utsuro.

00:51:58.080 --> 00:52:01.080
And end this ridiculous sob story
while I'm at it!

00:52:01.160 --> 00:52:03.830
But can you kill me?

00:52:04.620 --> 00:52:06.540
You wanted to save him, didn't you?

00:52:06.910 --> 00:52:08.910
You wanted to protect him, didn't you?

00:52:09.370 --> 00:52:13.750
I learned that all too well
on our travels here.

00:52:14.160 --> 00:52:16.290
If you kill your master for your friends,

00:52:16.450 --> 00:52:18.620
and then kill your friend
for your master...

00:52:18.950 --> 00:52:20.950
What will that leave you with?

00:52:21.540 --> 00:52:22.580
Nothing.

00:52:22.950 --> 00:52:26.750
You'll be nothing but a hollow void.

00:52:29.750 --> 00:52:34.290
Do you have what it takes
to live through that void?

00:52:45.950 --> 00:52:46.950
I...

00:52:47.750 --> 00:52:49.620
I will never be empty inside.

00:52:58.200 --> 00:53:00.250
What I wanted to protect

00:53:02.120 --> 00:53:03.750
is right here with me.

00:54:59.870 --> 00:55:02.370
Humans are hollow beings.

00:55:02.830 --> 00:55:07.120
But because they know that,
they take root in the hearts of others,

00:55:07.580 --> 00:55:10.580
never fading, even after death,

00:55:11.700 --> 00:55:15.790
and continue to live forever, is it?

00:55:42.700 --> 00:55:47.540
The score is now 246-247.

00:55:48.450 --> 00:55:51.620
How the mighty have fallen.

00:55:52.500 --> 00:55:54.410
This was our last duel,

00:55:54.500 --> 00:55:58.450
but I let someone else
fight in my stead and lost.

00:56:01.620 --> 00:56:03.950
It was your sword
that took him down.

00:56:04.910 --> 00:56:09.450
And the one who protected Shoyo
and me was you.

00:56:11.410 --> 00:56:15.910
Nothing could feel worse than a victory
given to me out of pity.

00:56:17.950 --> 00:56:22.750
I couldn't make you
cut Sensei down again.

00:56:24.660 --> 00:56:26.370
Compared to him,

00:56:26.750 --> 00:56:29.410
I was a much
easier target, wasn't I?

00:56:29.950 --> 00:56:31.040
Yeah.

00:56:31.410 --> 00:56:35.410
Ain't any other stupid mugs I've come
to love punching in as much as yours.

00:56:39.120 --> 00:56:41.200
It was the same when we were kids.

00:56:41.580 --> 00:56:43.700
We fought every time we met.

00:56:44.500 --> 00:56:48.950
I figured growing up
some would fix that,

00:56:50.160 --> 00:56:53.830
but we remained brats all the way.

00:56:54.370 --> 00:56:57.290
And in your case, you didn't even grow.

00:56:57.620 --> 00:56:58.700
I did.

00:57:01.120 --> 00:57:04.580
Maybe this is just
how we were fated to be.

00:57:05.700 --> 00:57:07.870
And that's not too bad.

00:57:08.700 --> 00:57:09.790
But, Takasugi,

00:57:10.540 --> 00:57:12.540
you know what?

00:57:14.160 --> 00:57:16.580
As much as we loved
to fight each other,

00:57:19.370 --> 00:57:20.790
I would've...

00:57:27.950 --> 00:57:30.950
loved to drink with you just as much.

00:57:41.290 --> 00:57:42.500
That's not us.

00:57:43.370 --> 00:57:45.040
Instead of wasting time on drinks,

00:57:45.620 --> 00:57:49.290
I would've used it to beat you
as many times as I could.

00:57:54.580 --> 00:57:57.580
But I'll give it a rest now.

00:57:58.370 --> 00:57:59.500
Get going.

00:58:01.950 --> 00:58:03.750
You aren't empty.

00:58:04.540 --> 00:58:05.700
You still have...

00:58:07.950 --> 00:58:11.830
plenty left to protect
with that thing, right?

00:58:13.250 --> 00:58:14.500
Takasugi...

00:58:15.330 --> 00:58:16.500
Gintoki,

00:58:17.500 --> 00:58:20.160
this crushed left eye of mine

00:58:21.160 --> 00:58:23.250
closed forever on that day,

00:58:23.330 --> 00:58:26.540
with the last thing it saw
etched into the back of its eyelid.

00:58:28.040 --> 00:58:32.290
I've lived my life staring at your gloomy
face from back then,

00:58:32.330 --> 00:58:33.950
and I'm sick of it.

00:58:35.540 --> 00:58:37.790
So at least when my right eye closes,

00:58:39.120 --> 00:58:43.120
don't go looking like
a goddamned fool.

00:58:45.500 --> 00:58:46.870
The kid...

00:58:47.250 --> 00:58:52.120
who stood tall before
me when we first met,

00:58:53.950 --> 00:58:56.500
the man I always wanted to beat,

00:58:58.160 --> 00:59:01.870
the man I spent my whole life
chasing,

00:59:02.750 --> 00:59:07.370
is better than that, isn't he?

00:59:16.700 --> 00:59:19.910
Wait for me in hell, Takasugi.

00:59:20.910 --> 00:59:22.580
I won't let you run away.

00:59:23.200 --> 00:59:25.330
I'll beat you for sure next time.

00:59:26.580 --> 00:59:28.160
Bring it on...

01:00:33.540 --> 01:00:34.540
Oh no!

01:00:34.790 --> 01:00:37.250
That ship sucked up too much Altana!

01:00:44.750 --> 01:00:46.500
Why are you helping me?

01:00:47.040 --> 01:00:50.370
I am the root cause
of all this calamity.

01:00:50.790 --> 01:00:51.950
If you see someone in need,

01:00:52.080 --> 01:00:54.830
help them out and then scram
with all their money.

01:00:55.080 --> 01:00:58.540
That's what Gintoki Sakata
has taught us over the years.

01:00:58.870 --> 01:00:59.870
Besides...

01:01:00.040 --> 01:01:01.910
I've always wanted to talk to the person

01:01:02.160 --> 01:01:04.250
who made him who he is.

01:01:04.950 --> 01:01:07.950
No, it's the other way around.

01:01:15.750 --> 01:01:20.160
If I hadn't met them, I would've
remained as empty as void.

01:01:22.410 --> 01:01:25.950
They made me human.

01:01:35.910 --> 01:01:41.330
But my existence only served
to shackle them down.

01:01:43.790 --> 01:01:46.700
I have no right
to call myself their teacher.

01:01:46.830 --> 01:01:47.950
Even so...

01:01:48.950 --> 01:01:50.870
Even if everything you said is true,

01:01:51.290 --> 01:01:55.250
it's because of you that
we got to meet Gintoki Sakata.

01:01:56.120 --> 01:01:57.870
I've always wanted to meet you

01:01:58.790 --> 01:02:00.040
and say...

01:02:00.870 --> 01:02:02.450
Thank you.

01:02:05.500 --> 01:02:07.830
I'm sure Gin and the others
feel the same way.

01:02:09.620 --> 01:02:11.750
Gintoki! Takasugi!

01:02:12.160 --> 01:02:15.580
Do you hear me? Are you all right?

01:02:16.450 --> 01:02:18.450
We've taken over Kuyo.

01:02:19.040 --> 01:02:20.830
The enemy is in tatters, too.

01:02:21.250 --> 01:02:24.330
But the Terminal is still
running out of control.

01:02:24.620 --> 01:02:27.450
It's only a matter of time before
it collapses with this ship.

01:02:27.750 --> 01:02:29.080
Get out of there at once!

01:02:29.250 --> 01:02:31.500
Zura! Running away won't help!

01:02:32.410 --> 01:02:36.750
If the Terminal goes down,
the Altana inside will go berserk.

01:02:37.040 --> 01:02:39.830
If worse comes to worst,
this entire planet could blow!

01:02:40.330 --> 01:02:43.330
But... is there nothing we can do?

01:02:44.790 --> 01:02:48.290
Could you let me handle this?

01:02:48.790 --> 01:02:50.620
Who are you?

01:02:52.040 --> 01:02:54.160
I'll use the weapons
on-board this ship.

01:02:54.830 --> 01:02:59.500
I'll fire all the Altana it has mined
back down via the Terminal,

01:03:00.370 --> 01:03:03.290
using the Altana within me.

01:03:03.750 --> 01:03:08.910
But even if that quells its rage,
the Terminal won't be left standing.

01:03:09.790 --> 01:03:12.410
Can I ask you to handle
the evacuations,

01:03:12.870 --> 01:03:15.120
my school's biggest prodigy?

01:03:16.290 --> 01:03:17.910
I know you can do it.

01:03:18.750 --> 01:03:20.540
You all should live on.

01:03:25.700 --> 01:03:27.200
All hands, evacuate!

01:03:27.330 --> 01:03:29.830
We're getting out of the Terminal
as quickly as we can!

01:03:30.450 --> 01:03:32.950
Zura! Use our ships!

01:03:33.580 --> 01:03:34.910
Well, there you have it.

01:03:35.870 --> 01:03:38.370
You should hurry up
and escape too.

01:03:39.620 --> 01:03:40.750
Shoyo-sensei!

01:03:42.370 --> 01:03:43.750
It's so ironic.

01:03:44.660 --> 01:03:49.700
I hated my eternal life,
but now time is not on my side.

01:03:50.580 --> 01:03:55.250
But that boy granted me
what little life I have left.

01:03:56.660 --> 01:03:59.500
They have paved the path
to the future...

01:04:02.040 --> 01:04:05.330
You are that future,
and it falls upon me to protect you all.

01:04:25.290 --> 01:04:28.410
Please last as long as you can, my life.
Every second counts.

01:04:28.790 --> 01:04:30.790
Mere seconds aren't enough.

01:04:32.580 --> 01:04:34.500
But if we add up all our lives,

01:04:34.700 --> 01:04:37.700
we can buy you enough time
to see your stupid student's face.

01:04:38.750 --> 01:04:39.790
You kids...

01:04:40.250 --> 01:04:42.830
We're sorry, but we really,

01:04:43.370 --> 01:04:45.120
really can't just leave like that.

01:04:45.790 --> 01:04:46.950
Didn't I say that?

01:04:47.040 --> 01:04:49.950
Our job isn't complete
until we scram with all your money.

01:04:51.830 --> 01:04:53.700
If the future's within our reach,

01:04:54.330 --> 01:04:56.290
then we'll grab it and scram.

01:04:58.580 --> 01:05:00.120
That's the Odd Jobs way.

01:05:00.540 --> 01:05:02.200
Let us join you, then.

01:05:02.870 --> 01:05:04.120
This sect...

01:05:04.370 --> 01:05:07.580
They'd been collecting
Altana from several planets

01:05:07.620 --> 01:05:10.040
to mass-produce their elixirs.

01:05:10.750 --> 01:05:14.540
If we fire it all in, then you'll
have time not just to see him,

01:05:14.830 --> 01:05:17.160
but even smack your
stupid student on the head.

01:05:17.540 --> 01:05:19.450
Fire it all in? How, exactly?

01:05:20.080 --> 01:05:21.160
Just so you know,

01:05:21.330 --> 01:05:23.790
I can't operate anything other
than my outdated cellphone.

01:05:23.910 --> 01:05:26.500
Modern tech's too overwhelming, right?

01:05:26.580 --> 01:05:28.790
Says the guy with the robot body.

01:05:28.950 --> 01:05:30.950
Well, leave that to me.

01:05:32.700 --> 01:05:34.620
Machines are the same as people.

01:05:35.250 --> 01:05:36.950
When they don't listen to you,

01:05:37.950 --> 01:05:39.540
you kick their ass!

01:05:44.370 --> 01:05:45.950
Hey, you crazies!

01:05:46.120 --> 01:05:48.830
All this violence
won't just get you blocked,

01:05:49.160 --> 01:05:51.750
it'll make even Siri snap
and start cussing us out!

01:05:52.080 --> 01:05:55.160
Oh, but all our feelings combined
are nothing to scoff at.

01:05:55.750 --> 01:05:58.450
Even without a cellphone,
they're sure to get through!

01:06:33.830 --> 01:06:34.830
Hey.

01:06:35.250 --> 01:06:36.330
You guys...

01:06:36.500 --> 01:06:38.870
Back on your feet.
Let's go!

01:06:41.040 --> 01:06:42.750
Gintoki, keep going.

01:06:43.160 --> 01:06:46.620
He... and the rest of the Odd Jobs
should be down that way.

01:06:47.330 --> 01:06:50.830
If there's anything you've left undone,
take care of it at once.

01:06:51.870 --> 01:06:54.410
O Mister Shoka Sonjuku's
Biggest Prodigy,

01:06:54.620 --> 01:06:57.660
weren't you tasked with
getting everyone to safety?

01:06:58.040 --> 01:07:00.040
Everyone has evacuated already...

01:07:00.450 --> 01:07:02.830
Other than you troublemakers, that is.

01:07:03.950 --> 01:07:06.120
Zura, Takasugi's...

01:07:07.040 --> 01:07:10.580
Perhaps Sensei didn't know...

01:07:12.910 --> 01:07:16.370
that back then,
whenever you two got up to mischief,

01:07:16.620 --> 01:07:19.450
there was another troublemaker

01:07:19.620 --> 01:07:22.500
cleaning up your messes.

01:07:25.620 --> 01:07:27.620
Isn't that right, Gintoki?

01:07:28.540 --> 01:07:32.040
If he... If you two are getting up
to one last act of mischief,

01:07:32.620 --> 01:07:37.620
then I can't leave this place
until I've cleaned up your mess.

01:07:39.160 --> 01:07:40.450
Zura...

01:07:41.410 --> 01:07:43.750
Live or die, we're in this together, eh?

01:07:44.160 --> 01:07:47.910
Then you have to make sure
you come back alive, eh, Gintoki?

01:07:48.250 --> 01:07:49.330
Relax!

01:07:49.790 --> 01:07:53.790
I'll rescue you from the depths of Hell
if I have to.

01:07:54.330 --> 01:07:55.330
So...

01:07:56.500 --> 01:07:58.580
Go raise all the hell you want...

01:08:01.330 --> 01:08:03.250
- Including our fallen friend's share!
- Including our fallen friend's share!

01:08:13.160 --> 01:08:14.540
Sogo!

01:08:47.620 --> 01:08:51.540
- Go!
- Go!

01:09:08.200 --> 01:09:12.540
Shoyo, I've always wanted
to show you this.

01:09:13.790 --> 01:09:17.290
A lot's happened
since back then, and now...

01:09:21.500 --> 01:09:24.500
I run an Odd Jobs business
with these guys.

01:09:30.500 --> 01:09:33.080
Yes, I got a good look,

01:09:33.620 --> 01:09:36.040
Odd Jobs Gintoki Sakata...

01:09:37.700 --> 01:09:40.700
You've grown into a fine man.

01:10:21.540 --> 01:10:22.620
Gintoki.

01:10:23.950 --> 01:10:28.330
The people here must be to you
what you were to me.

01:10:30.750 --> 01:10:34.080
Just as the eternal monster
from that day

01:10:34.290 --> 01:10:38.580
became human by meeting
you... meeting you kids,

01:10:40.330 --> 01:10:45.870
the little monster with
the sad eyes from that day

01:10:47.330 --> 01:10:50.500
has also become human, hasn't he?

01:11:23.750 --> 01:11:26.750
Data transfer complete.

01:11:33.410 --> 01:11:36.950
Good morning, Fuyo No. 0.

01:11:38.200 --> 01:11:39.660
Where am I?

01:11:40.200 --> 01:11:42.620
Master Gengai's robot warehouse.

01:11:43.580 --> 01:11:48.080
You were damaged in the war
and fell into a lengthy sleep.

01:11:49.330 --> 01:11:50.580
I'm your clone,

01:11:50.750 --> 01:11:54.040
and during that time,
I collected all the data for you.

01:11:54.330 --> 01:11:55.410
My name is Tamako.

01:11:55.950 --> 01:11:57.330
I'm very sorry...

01:11:57.750 --> 01:12:01.750
It seems my circuitry
is still a bit awry.

01:12:04.120 --> 01:12:06.950
How long did I spend asleep?

01:12:07.040 --> 01:12:08.160
"Part 3:"

01:12:08.290 --> 01:12:12.370
"Nobody with Naturally
Wavy Hair Can Be Trusted"

01:12:21.370 --> 01:12:23.040
Is this really Edo?

01:12:23.410 --> 01:12:25.950
No, it is called Tokyo now.

01:12:26.870 --> 01:12:28.500
Following the war,

01:12:28.580 --> 01:12:31.870
Edo was reborn and entered
a period of sustained development.

01:12:32.700 --> 01:12:34.620
But Tokyo wouldn't be what it is today

01:12:34.910 --> 01:12:37.410
without the efforts you all put in.

01:12:37.950 --> 01:12:40.950
So the world has returned to peace.

01:12:41.160 --> 01:12:44.330
"Welcome to Kabuki First District!"

01:12:45.330 --> 01:12:46.290
But...

01:12:46.830 --> 01:12:50.620
It no longer appears to be
the world I know.

01:12:55.620 --> 01:12:58.250
What became of everyone
after the war?

01:12:58.830 --> 01:13:01.750
You already know the answer to that.

01:13:02.290 --> 01:13:03.330
What?

01:13:15.750 --> 01:13:16.750
Tama.

01:13:17.450 --> 01:13:18.450
Tama?

01:13:19.410 --> 01:13:20.540
Shinpachi!

01:13:22.040 --> 01:13:24.160
When you finally wake up

01:13:24.620 --> 01:13:27.950
and obtain this data, who knows
how much time will have passed?

01:13:34.410 --> 01:13:36.080
Just what did we fight against?

01:13:36.410 --> 01:13:38.080
What did we defeat?

01:13:38.330 --> 01:13:40.290
Or were we defeated ourselves?

01:13:41.040 --> 01:13:44.790
There's still no clear answer to that,
but we did make it back.

01:13:45.620 --> 01:13:46.750
Back to Edo,

01:13:47.540 --> 01:13:48.910
and back to our usual
lives.

01:13:52.370 --> 01:13:56.410
But when I saw Gin's slightly
sad smile,

01:13:56.950 --> 01:13:58.830
I started to fully realize...

01:13:59.660 --> 01:14:01.790
the significance of the things
we'd regained

01:14:02.870 --> 01:14:04.870
and the things we'd lost.

01:14:17.950 --> 01:14:19.410
I wonder...

01:14:19.700 --> 01:14:20.950
if he'll be back...

01:14:25.410 --> 01:14:27.500
Where do you think you're sleeping, Gin?

01:14:27.620 --> 01:14:29.080
Ugh! I stepped on his puke!

01:14:29.250 --> 01:14:31.290
I was wondering
where you'd run off to,

01:14:31.330 --> 01:14:33.290
and you were out drinking
it up again?!

01:14:34.120 --> 01:14:36.950
Shut up. This is my own place.

01:14:37.250 --> 01:14:40.700
I'm free to come home when I want
and puke where I want.

01:14:41.250 --> 01:14:43.410
Hey! Don't make an even bigger mess—

01:14:45.540 --> 01:14:48.950
- I see.
- Who said you can take my seat?

01:14:49.250 --> 01:14:50.410
What are you talking about?

01:14:50.540 --> 01:14:53.790
I'm the leader because I kept Odd Jobs
going while you guys were away!

01:14:53.950 --> 01:14:56.870
And you're starting over as a lackey!
This was your idea!

01:14:56.950 --> 01:14:58.450
I said nothing of the sort.

01:14:58.580 --> 01:15:01.540
You were the one who said
you'd start over as a glasses frame.

01:15:01.830 --> 01:15:05.830
I did not say that! I think you need
to start over from your dad's skin!

01:15:05.950 --> 01:15:08.790
You go start over from
your old man's glasses case.

01:15:08.870 --> 01:15:10.620
That'd just make me
my old man's glasses!

01:15:10.750 --> 01:15:11.950
And just sleep in your bed...

01:15:12.450 --> 01:15:14.790
Don't just waltz into a lady's room!

01:15:15.540 --> 01:15:17.410
How many times
do I need to tell you?

01:15:17.540 --> 01:15:19.830
Since I came back second, I'm the COO,

01:15:19.910 --> 01:15:21.250
and this is my room now!

01:15:21.370 --> 01:15:25.040
Uh, COO? You blew away the
CEO too, you know?

01:15:25.830 --> 01:15:30.290
CEOs everywhere are just figureheads.
They're all Lay-Z good for nothings.

01:15:30.410 --> 01:15:33.620
The real power rests in the hands
of strong women like Goriki and myself.

01:15:34.160 --> 01:15:36.950
Might just makes right wherever you go.

01:15:37.080 --> 01:15:39.120
Goriki and you are very
different definitions of strong!

01:15:39.250 --> 01:15:40.700
And she was never a COO!

01:15:40.790 --> 01:15:43.950
Put that worthless fool
in the closet where he belongs.

01:15:45.540 --> 01:15:47.790
Uh, Goriki Muscles-Carter,
the closet was a no-go too.

01:15:48.080 --> 01:15:50.660
Damn it! Knock it off, you louts!

01:15:50.950 --> 01:15:52.620
Where do I belong in this place, then?

01:15:52.700 --> 01:15:55.410
Guess I'll go ahead
and mark all my spots.

01:15:55.830 --> 01:15:57.750
You wanna die, lackey?

01:15:58.080 --> 01:16:00.950
But still, we remain the same as always,

01:16:01.370 --> 01:16:05.160
and it must be because
all four of us are back together again.

01:16:10.500 --> 01:16:11.830
Good grief.

01:16:12.160 --> 01:16:15.370
I was hoping you'd have made a bunch
of money to pay off your rent,

01:16:15.620 --> 01:16:18.330
but it looks like two years passed

01:16:18.450 --> 01:16:20.620
while you were sitting
around picking your nose.

01:16:20.750 --> 01:16:23.700
I'll let the new CEO handle the rent.

01:16:23.950 --> 01:16:26.950
Could you not force me into the role
whenever things go south?

01:16:27.330 --> 01:16:28.950
Leave it to me, your leader.

01:16:29.120 --> 01:16:31.620
I'll handle the right nostril,
and Gin can take the left one.

01:16:31.750 --> 01:16:32.910
Shinpachi can do the rest.

01:16:32.950 --> 01:16:35.580
Do something other
than picking your nose!

01:16:35.700 --> 01:16:40.200
Idiots. And here I thought
Shinpachi and Kagura had grown.

01:16:40.370 --> 01:16:44.950
But the moment you come back,
they're right back to square one.

01:16:45.290 --> 01:16:50.200
One bad apple can
spoil the barrel, as they say.

01:16:50.330 --> 01:16:53.540
I'd rather be one of those sweet
canned apples than one in a barrel.

01:16:53.700 --> 01:16:54.950
Makes sense.

01:16:55.080 --> 01:16:56.160
If you're locked up in the can,

01:16:56.200 --> 01:16:58.330
you can go bad and it
won't affect the whole.

01:16:58.410 --> 01:17:00.700
Can we stop assuming
that I'm a bad apple?

01:17:01.200 --> 01:17:03.370
Everyone busted our balls,

01:17:03.750 --> 01:17:06.750
but nobody asked any questions
about why we came back here.

01:17:09.540 --> 01:17:11.540
Because the answer's already obvious.

01:17:12.450 --> 01:17:14.370
Let me ask you a question in turn.

01:17:14.830 --> 01:17:18.410
Why do I travel across space
to come see you here?

01:17:18.700 --> 01:17:20.910
- Because you're bald.
- Leave my scalp alone.

01:17:21.750 --> 01:17:23.620
Or maybe it's because...

01:17:23.790 --> 01:17:26.080
- you're bald.
- Again, that's not it.

01:17:26.750 --> 01:17:28.450
There's no particular reason.

01:17:29.080 --> 01:17:32.450
You don't need one to see family.

01:17:33.330 --> 01:17:34.790
This is the same.

01:17:35.200 --> 01:17:38.540
If you want to stay here
and be Odd Jobs again,

01:17:39.330 --> 01:17:41.500
you don't need a reason anymore.

01:17:42.950 --> 01:17:46.330
But that's also why
that disastrous brother of yours

01:17:46.660 --> 01:17:48.660
might show up here without a reason.

01:17:49.540 --> 01:17:53.700
Kagura said Umibozu looked a little sad
as he left with those words...

01:17:54.080 --> 01:17:56.700
and pretty damn bald.

01:17:58.250 --> 01:17:59.410
Well, whatever.

01:17:59.580 --> 01:18:02.580
I won't complain as long you as pay rent.

01:18:03.160 --> 01:18:05.250
They say we've entered
a new era and all.

01:18:05.370 --> 01:18:08.290
Surely there'll be some
good news to kick it off.

01:18:08.700 --> 01:18:10.910
- "EDO News: Rebuilding the Terminal"
- Have a look at this.

01:18:11.330 --> 01:18:14.450
Can you believe how well
the rebuild of the Terminal is going?

01:18:15.040 --> 01:18:17.200
No matter how many
obstacles we have to face,

01:18:17.330 --> 01:18:19.410
as long as we never give up,

01:18:19.910 --> 01:18:23.160
we should be able to get back up
as many times as it takes.

01:18:23.410 --> 01:18:25.450
So please, everyone...

01:18:25.540 --> 01:18:28.250
Princess Soyo, I hate to interrupt,
but we're here to ask you

01:18:28.330 --> 01:18:31.580
about the assassination of
former PM, Donald Zuramp.

01:18:31.620 --> 01:18:35.910
Rumors say you masterminded it.
Is it true?

01:18:41.790 --> 01:18:44.410
If you believe the princess
to be the kind of person

01:18:44.500 --> 01:18:46.250
to kill those in her way,

01:18:46.660 --> 01:18:50.950
then you stand here ready
to die, I take it?

01:18:51.120 --> 01:18:52.330
Nobume...

01:18:52.910 --> 01:18:56.620
A-An assassin!
Those rumors were true!

01:18:58.870 --> 01:19:00.870
Edo only managed to get back on its feet

01:19:01.200 --> 01:19:02.660
thanks to these girls.

01:19:03.370 --> 01:19:05.620
Actually, I'm sure they had on their side

01:19:05.870 --> 01:19:08.290
those three men, and...

01:19:09.250 --> 01:19:10.450
One more person.

01:19:11.950 --> 01:19:13.700
You fools!

01:19:13.910 --> 01:19:18.450
These little girls could never
do the great Zuramp in!

01:19:18.910 --> 01:19:22.830
That man continues to watch over
this nation as a heroic spirit!

01:19:23.200 --> 01:19:24.500
Never forget!

01:19:24.580 --> 01:19:27.080
If you stray from the right path,

01:19:27.200 --> 01:19:29.830
I will return to punish you!

01:19:29.950 --> 01:19:34.660
- I am the Heroic Patriot ObaZ!
- Heroic Patriot ObaZ

01:19:35.080 --> 01:19:37.330
And so, Katsura died.

01:19:37.410 --> 01:19:39.830
Don't take over the narration
and kill people off!

01:19:40.040 --> 01:19:42.660
We don't even know that's Katsura!

01:19:42.790 --> 01:19:44.290
It's obviously him, though!

01:19:44.410 --> 01:19:47.660
That idiot's already braindead.
Let him go.

01:19:47.910 --> 01:19:50.910
And this... narration thing
you've been doing? When's that gonna end?

01:19:51.120 --> 01:19:53.540
You heard all that?
Talk about embarrassing!

01:19:53.620 --> 01:19:57.250
No, I just wanted to make something
to tell Tama what happened.

01:19:57.790 --> 01:20:01.580
You trying to forcefully wrap up
this story with a sappy narration?

01:20:01.870 --> 01:20:03.500
Too long; didn't listen.

01:20:03.750 --> 01:20:05.750
You need to keep these things concise.

01:20:07.620 --> 01:20:08.620
Tama.

01:20:09.160 --> 01:20:10.830
A lot's happened since then,

01:20:11.370 --> 01:20:13.580
but I just want you to know this...

01:20:15.830 --> 01:20:18.500
- Everybody died.
- Don't take the easy way out!

01:20:18.750 --> 01:20:21.250
What's the problem?
Everyone dies eventually.

01:20:21.330 --> 01:20:22.620
It's too lazy!

01:20:22.700 --> 01:20:25.500
Tama will want more details
on what happened!

01:20:25.830 --> 01:20:27.620
Shinpachi's right.

01:20:28.120 --> 01:20:30.620
Everything that happened
while she wasn't around,

01:20:30.750 --> 01:20:32.160
and the emotions we felt...

01:20:32.500 --> 01:20:34.620
I want her to know all of it.

01:20:36.830 --> 01:20:38.540
The egg rolls were yum.

01:20:38.620 --> 01:20:40.330
Nobody gives a solitary shit!

01:20:41.580 --> 01:20:43.290
I hope you saw all that.

01:20:44.160 --> 01:20:46.500
"Without supervision,
people will even stoop

01:20:46.620 --> 01:20:47.950
- to falsifying endings."
- Who?

01:20:47.950 --> 01:20:49.370
Not me!

01:20:49.870 --> 01:20:52.120
Society needs watchful eyes

01:20:52.250 --> 01:20:55.120
that can monitor people
and nations across eras.

01:20:55.330 --> 01:20:57.950
And the only one capable
of that is the Heroic Spirit...

01:20:58.200 --> 01:21:00.040
ObaZ, and ObaZ alone!

01:21:05.040 --> 01:21:08.200
We ignore him,
and he even sneaks in here?

01:21:08.370 --> 01:21:10.660
Either way, that takes care
of one problem.

01:21:10.790 --> 01:21:12.040
Who's next?

01:21:12.120 --> 01:21:14.790
Quit trying to force
an everbody died ending!

01:21:15.250 --> 01:21:16.250
And that...

01:21:16.410 --> 01:21:18.250
would be the last time
he played the straight man.

01:21:18.330 --> 01:21:19.870
I'm not dead!

01:21:20.950 --> 01:21:23.410
Don't worry! I'm not handing
over the narration!

01:21:24.040 --> 01:21:26.660
The Zuramp Administration handed
things over to the next generation,

01:21:26.870 --> 01:21:31.750
and with that, the Shinsengumi
returned to power.

01:21:32.330 --> 01:21:34.830
I'd like to say, Welcome back,

01:21:35.750 --> 01:21:37.830
but what you've returned to...

01:21:38.580 --> 01:21:39.950
is a warzone.

01:21:40.750 --> 01:21:42.750
Are you prepared to die?

01:21:44.620 --> 01:21:48.540
Then drink until you drop!

01:21:53.660 --> 01:21:56.660
There are no breaks in their war.

01:21:57.330 --> 01:22:00.950
A life like that can get
overwhelming at times,

01:22:01.160 --> 01:22:04.580
but they'll be fine,
because they have her.

01:22:05.450 --> 01:22:08.950
The woman who once rebuffed
all the moves Kondo tried on her

01:22:09.410 --> 01:22:12.330
now supports him wholly in both
his professional and personal life.

01:22:13.040 --> 01:22:17.660
I'm a little saddened by that,
but I'll accept it for Sis's happiness.

01:22:18.620 --> 01:22:20.790
Ah, maybe I have
grown from boy to man.

01:22:22.450 --> 01:22:25.080
Have a taste of the straight
man's comeback, then!

01:22:25.370 --> 01:22:28.540
Are you the one bullshiting the narration?

01:22:28.620 --> 01:22:29.950
Just kidding.

01:22:30.160 --> 01:22:32.040
It's just, when I see my
future brother-in-law,

01:22:32.330 --> 01:22:33.700
I get this urge to play around with him.

01:22:33.790 --> 01:22:35.580
Stop that. I'm right here.

01:22:35.830 --> 01:22:37.750
And you, Sis!

01:22:37.950 --> 01:22:40.450
Why are you going along
with the fake narration?

01:22:40.540 --> 01:22:42.950
Huh? I did nothing of the sort.

01:22:43.370 --> 01:22:44.910
I was just...

01:22:51.580 --> 01:22:52.950
Yo, Gorilla.

01:22:53.620 --> 01:22:55.080
Didn't I say you'd
have to pay triple price

01:22:55.120 --> 01:22:57.580
if you showed your face here again?

01:22:57.700 --> 01:23:00.500
You were saying some crazy things
during the narration!

01:23:00.700 --> 01:23:01.620
Yes.

01:23:01.750 --> 01:23:04.830
My wallet—No, the government's coffers...

01:23:05.120 --> 01:23:06.580
belong to you now.

01:23:06.830 --> 01:23:08.290
Take this.

01:23:08.500 --> 01:23:10.410
It's a B'z concert ticket.

01:23:10.620 --> 01:23:13.790
Damn, Gorilla, you're naughty.

01:23:14.160 --> 01:23:15.500
Not as much as you, Otae.

01:23:15.620 --> 01:23:18.040
This is just footage
of official corruption!

01:23:18.200 --> 01:23:20.040
You used the narration to hide it, huh?

01:23:20.160 --> 01:23:22.620
Hey. You ate up all that screen time,

01:23:22.790 --> 01:23:26.290
and what you did is still stupid,
what did you do, idiots?

01:23:26.410 --> 01:23:29.660
Master, that was a bit better, no?

01:23:30.500 --> 01:23:33.370
I don't need a fake narration,

01:23:34.080 --> 01:23:35.750
as long as I have this.

01:23:36.450 --> 01:23:39.410
You're wrapping things up?
Okay, you get one minute.

01:23:40.620 --> 01:23:41.830
"Special Police Shinsengumi"

01:23:41.910 --> 01:23:44.120
Things went back
to how they used to be.

01:23:44.450 --> 01:23:45.790
But that only signaled...

01:23:45.910 --> 01:23:49.910
the start of a new battle
for the Shinsengumi.

01:23:50.120 --> 01:23:51.410
Special: Shinsengumi Kenpucho

01:23:51.540 --> 01:23:54.450
Forget ending, we're getting
a new preview!

01:23:54.830 --> 01:23:56.910
What is the Shinsengumi's new battle?

01:23:57.080 --> 01:23:58.750
Who is their new foe?

01:23:58.830 --> 01:24:01.450
That's not new at all!
We saw him earlier!

01:24:01.620 --> 01:24:03.540
What is the Shinsengumi's new weapon?

01:24:03.580 --> 01:24:04.700
- Hey, what happened...
- "Sagaru Yamazaki Develops..."

01:24:04.750 --> 01:24:06.250
- to Blandy?
- "108 split personalities when revived!"

01:24:07.700 --> 01:24:11.080
It ain't easy being Vice Chief, huh?

01:24:11.950 --> 01:24:14.540
But I'll keep the Shinsengumi going,

01:24:14.870 --> 01:24:16.830
just like you would have...

01:24:17.870 --> 01:24:18.910
Hijikata...

01:24:19.290 --> 01:24:22.080
You're falsifying the narration too?

01:24:22.410 --> 01:24:24.750
What do you louts think
you're doing instead of working?

01:24:24.870 --> 01:24:27.330
Kill yourselves to atone
for your lack of discipline!

01:24:27.450 --> 01:24:30.540
Hijikata, everything's over
after this movie.

01:24:30.830 --> 01:24:32.750
We won't get paid for any extra work.

01:24:33.120 --> 01:24:34.540
I mean, just look at Yamazaki.

01:24:34.790 --> 01:24:37.250
He's playing mechabaddi
with the Mechazakis.

01:24:37.330 --> 01:24:40.040
Again... What the hell is mechabaddi?

01:24:40.080 --> 01:24:42.450
What the hell are Mechazakis?!

01:24:42.580 --> 01:24:43.950
Vice Chief, Vice Chief!

01:24:44.160 --> 01:24:47.330
We get that none of you guys
have any idea how to wrap things up.

01:24:47.500 --> 01:24:48.790
Just take this.

01:24:49.580 --> 01:24:50.750
Now pose.

01:24:51.700 --> 01:24:52.950
Good. Keep it up.

01:24:59.500 --> 01:25:00.910
Don't just walk away!

01:25:01.250 --> 01:25:03.410
Why the hell did you make me do this?

01:25:03.500 --> 01:25:05.910
The Shinsengumi was... y'know.

01:25:06.040 --> 01:25:09.330
"Y'know" what? Who sums
anything up like that?

01:25:09.620 --> 01:25:12.790
Don't be so on edge, Hijikata.

01:25:12.950 --> 01:25:14.500
This is the end. Take it easy.

01:25:14.580 --> 01:25:16.700
There is no end to the police's job!

01:25:16.830 --> 01:25:17.910
I see.

01:25:17.950 --> 01:25:20.160
So it's the police's job
to shout and cause mayhem

01:25:20.290 --> 01:25:21.830
at a private establishment?

01:25:21.950 --> 01:25:24.910
If so, then I shall do my job as well.

01:25:25.040 --> 01:25:26.370
Kyubei...

01:25:26.500 --> 01:25:29.950
Go on, then. What is your job?

01:25:30.160 --> 01:25:31.700
Why don't you show me...

01:25:31.950 --> 01:25:33.410
Fruit platter.

01:25:33.500 --> 01:25:35.750
- Say aah.
- Aah.

01:25:35.950 --> 01:25:37.700
Wait, your job's cabaret girl?!

01:25:37.790 --> 01:25:41.700
When I invited her to come hang out,
she insisted on helping.

01:25:41.950 --> 01:25:45.410
I came up with a way to serve men
without approaching them.

01:25:45.790 --> 01:25:47.700
I can be ranked number one with this!

01:25:47.830 --> 01:25:49.950
Don't make a girl who measures
personal space with her sword

01:25:50.080 --> 01:25:51.910
serve patrons!

01:25:52.120 --> 01:25:53.450
It's a sales tactic.

01:25:53.750 --> 01:25:56.620
In Yoshiwara,
they often play hard-to-get,

01:25:56.830 --> 01:25:59.580
making the customers
more obsessed with them!

01:26:04.160 --> 01:26:06.120
Otae.
Cleanup completed.

01:26:06.200 --> 01:26:09.040
Forget hard-to-get,
this is hard-to-survive!

01:26:10.080 --> 01:26:11.700
Gin... You can't...

01:26:11.830 --> 01:26:15.450
And I have zero idea
what this idiot's trying to do!

01:26:15.540 --> 01:26:18.370
Hey, I came to hang out like you asked,

01:26:18.500 --> 01:26:20.540
but there are no uggos here.

01:26:21.450 --> 01:26:23.370
There's your order.

01:26:23.750 --> 01:26:25.370
Tsukky! Kyu!

01:26:25.540 --> 01:26:26.660
Kagura.

01:26:26.870 --> 01:26:28.250
Have you been well?

01:26:28.370 --> 01:26:30.790
Yup! You were all here, huh?

01:26:30.950 --> 01:26:33.080
Yes. All of us.

01:26:35.950 --> 01:26:38.500
Talk about a self-centered bunch.

01:26:38.950 --> 01:26:41.540
They all show up to bask
in the ending's spotlight.

01:26:42.790 --> 01:26:45.870
But now, we can wrap up
all their stories in the narration.

01:26:46.250 --> 01:26:48.700
How do we do that, exactly?

01:26:48.950 --> 01:26:51.450
Everybody got black-out
drunk together?

01:26:51.750 --> 01:26:53.200
Hey, that doesn't sound too bad.

01:26:53.330 --> 01:26:55.580
It suits us perfectly, does it not?

01:26:57.700 --> 01:26:59.620
Yeah... Same as always.

01:27:00.580 --> 01:27:03.950
That might just be the perfect
phrase for us.

01:27:04.410 --> 01:27:06.330
Come on, keep it together!

01:27:06.450 --> 01:27:09.830
Hey! What makes you think I'm not?

01:27:10.410 --> 01:27:14.500
Want me to list all of Dragon Ball's
adversaries to prove it

01:27:14.750 --> 01:27:17.830
By saying that,
you already proved that you don't!

01:27:18.410 --> 01:27:20.330
Doctor G—

01:27:20.450 --> 01:27:21.750
Hey, lady.

01:27:22.160 --> 01:27:23.950
Ten more of this.

01:27:24.160 --> 01:27:26.660
Come on, give it a rest.

01:27:26.750 --> 01:27:30.620
We're poor now.
We don't have any backers.

01:27:30.950 --> 01:27:33.370
But food on Earth is so good.

01:27:33.790 --> 01:27:37.330
Besides, they say you can't
fight on an empty stomach.

01:27:38.290 --> 01:27:41.950
Fight? We can't afford to.

01:27:42.330 --> 01:27:44.830
Then... I'll look forward
to when we can.

01:27:45.040 --> 01:27:46.370
Here, lady.

01:27:48.620 --> 01:27:51.330
Next time, I'll come to feast
on Earth itself.

01:27:51.700 --> 01:27:54.950
Yeesh. That's some big words.

01:27:55.410 --> 01:27:57.830
Dream big, money or no money.

01:27:58.200 --> 01:28:00.250
You nincompoop.

01:28:01.700 --> 01:28:03.910
- G-Good job noticing us!
- "Well done!"

01:28:03.950 --> 01:28:05.370
"(lol)"

01:28:13.080 --> 01:28:15.370
"Odd Jobs Gin"

01:28:15.450 --> 01:28:18.200
"From Tatsuma Sakamoto"

01:28:18.580 --> 01:28:21.950
"We haven't talked in a while."

01:28:22.080 --> 01:28:24.250
"How have you been,"

01:28:24.540 --> 01:28:25.950
"Peentoki?"

01:28:26.250 --> 01:28:30.160
"I'm flying across
the universe as always."

01:28:30.750 --> 01:28:33.160
"Space really is the best."

01:28:33.410 --> 01:28:37.290
"You should join me
on a trip sometime, Cuntoki."

01:28:37.950 --> 01:28:40.080
"The reason I'm writing to you"

01:28:40.410 --> 01:28:43.500
"is because I have something to say."

01:28:44.950 --> 01:28:46.160
"That day,"

01:28:46.410 --> 01:28:50.450
"I promised to rescue you all,"

01:28:50.830 --> 01:28:53.080
"but when I saw
the Terminal crumble down,"

01:28:53.200 --> 01:28:56.080
"'they ded lololol'"

01:28:56.620 --> 01:28:58.290
"was my first thought."

01:29:02.950 --> 01:29:05.120
"I don't mean this as consolation
or anything."

01:29:05.330 --> 01:29:10.330
"I truly believe he saved you back then."

01:29:11.370 --> 01:29:14.330
"So you don't need to
beat yourself up over it."

01:29:14.870 --> 01:29:19.160
"Your teacher's soul lives on
everywhere on Earth,"

01:29:19.410 --> 01:29:23.290
"and he continues
to watch over you, I'm sure."

01:29:24.160 --> 01:29:26.370
"To my beloved friend,"

01:29:26.830 --> 01:29:29.040
"Peencunfuku."

01:29:29.790 --> 01:29:33.790
"P.S. here's something I heard
when I ran into Zura the other day."

01:29:34.200 --> 01:29:38.160
"The remnants of the Kiheitai
are making strange moves, it seems."

01:29:39.620 --> 01:29:41.040
"The gates?"

01:29:41.330 --> 01:29:42.330
"Indeed."

01:29:42.410 --> 01:29:44.500
"Who do you think you're mimicking?"

01:29:44.910 --> 01:29:50.290
"She probably couldn't stand the fact
that she was so powerless."

01:29:51.700 --> 01:29:53.620
"But she was thankful"

01:29:53.910 --> 01:29:58.290
"that she could see him smile again
after he was a prisoner was so long."

01:30:01.620 --> 01:30:03.040
"And she says..."

01:30:03.200 --> 01:30:06.200
"it's her turn now."

01:30:07.950 --> 01:30:12.370
"There is no chance of him
coming back to life like Utsuro did."

01:30:12.750 --> 01:30:15.250
"That was a miracle which only occurred"

01:30:15.330 --> 01:30:17.700
"because Utsuro was born from Altana."

01:30:18.700 --> 01:30:20.950
"That's just fine."

01:30:21.580 --> 01:30:23.120
"This is how we,"

01:30:24.200 --> 01:30:26.910
"the Kiheitai, atone for our sins."

01:30:28.620 --> 01:30:31.160
"Takechi... You too?"

01:30:32.370 --> 01:30:34.370
"You're abandoning me too?"

01:30:45.620 --> 01:30:47.750
"Here's what I believe."

01:30:48.290 --> 01:30:51.540
"Miracles aren't real."

01:31:09.200 --> 01:31:11.790
"When a teacher
protects his student,"

01:31:16.120 --> 01:31:18.160
"you can't call that a miracle."

01:31:23.120 --> 01:31:24.660
"That's..."

01:31:24.830 --> 01:31:27.370
"just what they do."

01:31:31.910 --> 01:31:34.450
"Ken Shimura"

01:31:35.370 --> 01:31:37.160
Oh, you're here?

01:31:39.040 --> 01:31:42.040
It's been a while since
we came to see Father together.

01:31:43.040 --> 01:31:44.870
Do you have any news for him?

01:31:45.330 --> 01:31:46.250
Nah.

01:31:46.330 --> 01:31:49.870
As he died, our father lamented
the state of Edo's skies,

01:31:57.250 --> 01:32:01.620
but to me, even these same old skies
look a tad different now.

01:32:09.830 --> 01:32:13.290
After all, we know...

01:32:14.500 --> 01:32:17.620
that the people we care about
live under these skies.

01:32:24.950 --> 01:32:27.370
They might get cloudy at times,

01:32:27.950 --> 01:32:29.950
but in our hearts...

01:32:30.790 --> 01:32:35.790
Beneath my skies live
all the people I love so much.

01:32:49.580 --> 01:32:50.580
So, Tama,

01:32:51.330 --> 01:32:55.250
even if you find yourself
beneath unfamiliar skies,

01:32:56.620 --> 01:32:58.040
please don't cry.

01:32:59.120 --> 01:33:02.950
We'll always remain
in your heart with you.

01:33:04.540 --> 01:33:06.540
And if you'll believe in that,

01:33:08.040 --> 01:33:09.750
then I'm sure...

01:33:09.950 --> 01:33:12.620
we'll come to you
and wipe your tears away.

01:33:15.370 --> 01:33:18.200
"Odd Jobs Gin"
"Snack Otose"

01:33:31.750 --> 01:33:33.040
Let's keep going.

01:33:36.250 --> 01:33:41.750
-After that, these girls went on
to live as citizens of the modern age.

01:33:42.410 --> 01:33:44.950
The world was entering
a golden age of technology.

01:33:45.330 --> 01:33:49.330
Machines, and not people,
were to be the new leaders.

01:33:51.200 --> 01:33:53.950
These girls were robots,
so they lived happy lives.

01:33:55.700 --> 01:33:57.700
And humans...

01:33:58.830 --> 01:34:00.410
ended up unemployed.

01:34:00.700 --> 01:34:02.620
Each and every one of them.

01:34:02.870 --> 01:34:06.790
If nobody has a job, they can't call
anyone out for being unemployed.

01:34:06.950 --> 01:34:08.580
The jobless will blend in.

01:34:08.750 --> 01:34:11.750
Everyone will be happy.

01:34:11.950 --> 01:34:15.410
Every single person... can be happy...

01:34:15.540 --> 01:34:17.330
Mister Hasegawa?

01:34:17.660 --> 01:34:19.620
Why's he here in the future?

01:34:21.620 --> 01:34:25.450
Tamako, let me tell you
how this story really ends.

01:34:25.540 --> 01:34:27.950
- "Unemployed. State: Dangerously Drunk"
- Edo's going to turn into... hic...

01:34:29.040 --> 01:34:32.750
Number 0... the data I gave you
might have contained

01:34:32.830 --> 01:34:34.290
some massive errors!

01:34:34.330 --> 01:34:35.750
Massive errors?

01:34:39.250 --> 01:34:42.750
- You're bullshitting the narration too?
- You're bullshitting the narration too?

01:34:43.290 --> 01:34:45.950
What the hell did you tell Tamako?!

01:34:46.040 --> 01:34:47.160
No!

01:34:47.500 --> 01:34:50.950
I was just saying how hard it was to
find work after I quit being the hero...

01:34:51.160 --> 01:34:55.040
My apologies. This world we perceived

01:34:55.200 --> 01:34:58.910
was bugged out by the inclusion
of Hasegawa's data.

01:35:02.620 --> 01:35:04.370
The real world...

01:35:10.160 --> 01:35:11.950
-Hey. Good morning.

01:35:14.250 --> 01:35:16.540
You still look half-asleep.

01:35:17.410 --> 01:35:18.540
Whatever.

01:35:18.700 --> 01:35:21.290
We've got some urgent work
to take care of.

01:35:21.870 --> 01:35:23.500
Let's catch up later.

01:35:23.750 --> 01:35:25.580
Huh? Wait, Gin!

01:35:28.250 --> 01:35:31.870
Oh, and... you don't need us to
wipe those tears away, right?

01:35:33.200 --> 01:35:37.370
Looks like the clouds upstairs
have stopped crying, too.

01:35:38.200 --> 01:35:40.200
The skies have cleared up.

01:35:44.290 --> 01:35:45.450
Let's go.

01:35:52.250 --> 01:35:54.450
Hey, Gin, where are we going?

01:35:54.580 --> 01:35:56.450
What's this urgent work we have?

01:35:57.040 --> 01:35:59.750
- What was it?
- You forgot? Wasn't it urgent?!

01:35:59.870 --> 01:36:01.410
What was it, Leader?

01:36:01.540 --> 01:36:02.660
Beats me.

01:36:02.830 --> 01:36:05.330
Well, hey, it doesn't matter what.

01:36:07.290 --> 01:36:09.040
After all,

01:36:10.080 --> 01:36:11.700
we're the Odd Jobs!

01:36:20.370 --> 01:36:28.870
GINTAMA
The final

01:40:09.120 --> 01:40:11.750
- "Teach us, Ginpachi-sensei"
- Class 3-Z...

01:40:12.040 --> 01:40:15.040
Teach us, Ginpachi-sensei!

01:40:15.540 --> 01:40:18.330
Stand, bow, take your seats.

01:40:18.790 --> 01:40:19.830
Listen up, kids.

01:40:19.950 --> 01:40:22.290
Both the manga and movie
have reached the final chapter.

01:40:22.370 --> 01:40:25.750
So you guys, who'd been repeating
year after year, finally get to graduate too.

01:40:25.870 --> 01:40:29.200
On that note, say hello to the new
transfer student, Hideaki Sorachi.

01:40:29.620 --> 01:40:32.910
He says you can ask him
anything right now and he'll answer.

01:40:33.250 --> 01:40:36.370
Sensei! How are we supposed to
communite with a gorilla?!

01:40:36.540 --> 01:40:38.910
What's he saying?
All I hear is "ooh".

01:40:39.370 --> 01:40:40.450
- Me too?
- Sensei,

01:40:40.660 --> 01:40:44.200
a place with multiple gorillas
is a zoo, not a school.

01:40:44.330 --> 01:40:45.950
- May I go home?
-Okay, I get it.

01:40:46.080 --> 01:40:48.120
Kondo, Sorachi, and Otae,
go home to your cages now.

01:40:49.500 --> 01:40:50.500
Excuse me.

01:40:50.700 --> 01:40:53.200
I can interpret for you
if you'd like, Sensei.

01:40:53.330 --> 01:40:54.660
You're the Sensei, Shoyo.

01:40:54.790 --> 01:40:56.950
As someone who's been
repeating eternity,

01:40:57.120 --> 01:40:58.870
I can understand their language.

01:40:58.950 --> 01:41:01.250
A guy who repeats forever
is just an idiot, Shoyo.

01:41:01.370 --> 01:41:02.950
This is the question Kondo has:

01:41:03.660 --> 01:41:06.750
Getting kicked off of Jump,
two final chapter scams,

01:41:06.910 --> 01:41:09.290
and multiple delays...
Why did all that happen?

01:41:09.370 --> 01:41:12.330
I would never ask such a dangerous
question! He really is an idiot, Sensei!

01:41:13.500 --> 01:41:15.620
Oh, I see. Is that what happened?

01:41:15.750 --> 01:41:17.750
Sensei! You didn't need
an interpreter after all?!

01:41:17.830 --> 01:41:20.660
It's a delicate matter,
so I'll bananacoat it.

01:41:20.790 --> 01:41:22.750
Sugarcoat it instead, Sensei.

01:41:22.790 --> 01:41:24.200
- "I was busy playing Sekiro"
- It's like this.

01:41:24.330 --> 01:41:27.950
Sensei! The banana peel isn't working!
The Sekiro is there for all to see!

01:41:28.080 --> 01:41:29.080
Forget the banana.

01:41:29.120 --> 01:41:32.290
It seems things got crazy after Isshin
tore his way out of Genichiro's back.

01:41:32.370 --> 01:41:35.120
Stop talking about Sekiro.
It'll cause online drama.

01:41:35.410 --> 01:41:37.950
- Anybody else got questions?
- I'm too scared to ask!

01:41:38.200 --> 01:41:39.120
Me, Sensei.

01:41:39.160 --> 01:41:41.790
We never got any details
about Gintoki Sakata's origins.

01:41:41.910 --> 01:41:43.330
Who is he, actually?

01:41:43.500 --> 01:41:46.950
There's a fan theory that says
he's half-Amanto due to having silver hair.

01:41:47.160 --> 01:41:48.830
Does that mean Sacchan
with her purple hair

01:41:48.910 --> 01:41:50.950
is half-Osakan hag?

01:41:51.120 --> 01:41:53.750
Rude! And how can you even be
half an Osakan hag?

01:41:53.870 --> 01:41:56.580
Don't worry, Sarutobi.
You aren't an Osakan hag.

01:41:56.750 --> 01:41:58.290
You're only halfway there,
so Nagoyan hag.

01:41:58.330 --> 01:41:59.290
So I'm still a hag?!

01:41:59.330 --> 01:42:01.580
Does that mean
the silver-haired man is...

01:42:01.700 --> 01:42:03.750
...half-Sugamo geezer?

01:42:04.370 --> 01:42:06.290
I hate to say it,
but you're all wrong.

01:42:06.370 --> 01:42:07.370
Keep it between us,

01:42:07.450 --> 01:42:10.120
but the bananacoated
reason for the silver hair is...

01:42:10.250 --> 01:42:12.330
- "Because manga"
- Too blunt, Sensei!

01:42:12.450 --> 01:42:13.910
Do your damn job, banana peel!

01:42:14.160 --> 01:42:15.700
Any other questions?

01:42:15.750 --> 01:42:17.910
Enough, Sensei!
We'll just dig our own graves!

01:42:18.080 --> 01:42:21.700
Okay. I shall turn
everything hollow, then,

01:42:21.870 --> 01:42:23.580
with this one question to end them all.

01:42:23.620 --> 01:42:24.580
Bad news, Sensei.

01:42:24.660 --> 01:42:27.790
Shoyo's other persona,
Hollow Brain has come out.

01:42:28.040 --> 01:42:30.330
He's going to ask something real bad!

01:42:30.830 --> 01:42:32.200
Sorachi, do you...

01:42:32.410 --> 01:42:34.290
...count bananas as snacks?

01:42:34.370 --> 01:42:36.700
- Whoa, it's Shoyo!
- Stay out of this, Shoyo!

01:42:36.830 --> 01:42:40.120
What I want to ask is,
do you count bananas as royalties?

01:42:40.200 --> 01:42:42.410
Nah, bananas count as snacks, right?

01:42:42.500 --> 01:42:44.330
Looks like both their questions
are trash.

01:42:44.410 --> 01:42:46.330
- Banana is royalties!
- Banana is a snack!

01:42:46.410 --> 01:42:49.040
Somebody stop those two...
I mean, that one moron.

01:42:49.290 --> 01:42:50.370
Any other questions?

01:42:50.410 --> 01:42:53.080
Sensei! What was that ObaZ
stuff all about?

01:42:53.120 --> 01:42:54.660
You need to drop it already.

01:42:55.500 --> 01:42:58.370
Sensei. In the end, am I dead?

01:42:58.580 --> 01:43:00.290
Or am I alive? Which is it?

01:43:00.410 --> 01:43:04.910
It's Takasugi! The one whose survival
was left up in the air in the movie!

01:43:05.790 --> 01:43:09.620
It was obviously left vague
so people could have hope.

01:43:09.700 --> 01:43:13.540
Are you prepared to accept reality,
cruel as it may be?

01:43:14.410 --> 01:43:15.450
Yeah.

01:43:15.620 --> 01:43:17.580
"Okay, I'll just be honest and say"

01:43:17.620 --> 01:43:19.200
- "I didn't want to waste pages on that."
- Too blunt!

01:43:19.290 --> 01:43:20.750
- "Rather than expand on Takasugi's fate,"
- Bananacoat it!

01:43:20.790 --> 01:43:22.040
"I wanted to fit in
as many jokes as I could."

01:43:22.120 --> 01:43:23.540
Not that I care,

01:43:23.830 --> 01:43:26.540
but we can decide if
Takasugi's alive or dead by vote.

01:43:26.620 --> 01:43:28.410
Don't use democracy
to decide one's fate!

01:43:28.580 --> 01:43:32.790
Okay. Was that bare butt Takasugi's ass
or some random kid's ass?

01:43:32.870 --> 01:43:33.910
Pick what you like.

01:43:33.950 --> 01:43:36.080
Sensei, why are there two votes already?

01:43:36.370 --> 01:43:38.080
- Sekiro for me, then.
- Me too!

01:43:38.200 --> 01:43:39.410
- Sensei.
- Me three.

01:43:39.500 --> 01:43:41.410
One vote for everybody died.

01:43:41.500 --> 01:43:44.200
"FIN"

01:43:44.330 --> 01:43:46.950
Voice Cast
Hideaki Sorachi: Hideaki Sorachi
